Subject: sunxi: H713: start V2 HDMI input on normal boots

Run the V2 HDMI startup from PREBOOT instead of the logo-only sequence.
Use the bench board's RTC GP6 launch latch: after power loss (0) or a
boot whose HDMI start Linux acknowledged (HDOK), write HDMI, launch the
display firmware once with the CPU_COMM trace, select source 3 and boot
Linux with the handoff. Any other latch value, or a running MIPS core,
takes the existing logo-only path.

A failure after the latch is set resets the SoC rather than launching
the firmware a second time in one boot. The latch sends the next boot
down the logo-only path. PREBOOT runs before bootmeth_rauc, so no slot
attempt is used.

Publish the handoff from ft_board_setup() as /chosen/h713,hdmi-boot-v1,
so the slot's boot.scr and FIT stay unchanged, and only to a V2 tree that
describes the HDMI resources (kernel 0218). The running firmware keeps
writing its CPU_COMM trace page, so add a /memreserve/ for it when an
older slot's tree does not reserve it. Keep the PID out of the
environment on normal boots: bootmeth_rauc saves it, and a stale PID
must never reach a later boot.
